rules_jvm_external fix: pin each artifact to the repository that served it.

`private/rules/coursier.bzl` records every configured repository as a
`mirror_urls` entry for every artifact, so the v3 lock file lists each artifact
under both `maven.google.com` and `repo1.maven.org`. At build time
`http_file` tries the URLs in repository order, so an artifact that exists only
on Maven Central is first requested from Google Maven, which answers 404 and
makes Bazel print `WARNING: Download from https://maven.google.com/... 404`
for every such artifact on a cold build.

Coursier already knows the URL it actually downloaded from (`primary_url`).
Recording only that repository keeps the lock honest, removes the cold-build
404 warnings, and still fails loudly if that one repository stops serving the
artifact instead of silently falling back to a different copy.

--- a/private/rules/coursier.bzl
+++ b/private/rules/coursier.bzl
@@ -1393,12 +1393,10 @@
                 repository_urls.append(r["repo_url"].rstrip("/"))
         primary_artifact_path = infer_artifact_path_from_primary_and_repos(primary_url, repository_urls)
 
-        mirror_urls = [url + "/" + primary_artifact_path for url in repository_urls]
-        if primary_url in mirror_urls:
-            # http_file tries URLs in order, so putting the URL that actually worked first
-            # minimizes repository fetch 404s. See: https://github.com/bazelbuild/rules_jvm_external/issues/349
-            mirror_urls = [primary_url] + [url for url in mirror_urls if url != primary_url]
-        artifact.update({"mirror_urls": mirror_urls})
+        # Only the repository that actually served the artifact. Listing every
+        # configured repository as a mirror makes http_file probe the missing
+        # ones first and log a WARNING per 404 on each cold build.
+        artifact.update({"mirror_urls": [primary_url]})
 
         files_to_inspect.append(repository_ctx.path(artifact["file"]))
 
